From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: esp32s31: describe 32 MiB of PSRAM

The Function-CoreBoard comes with 16 or 32 MiB of PSRAM. U-Boot's SPL
detects the size and maps all of it; Linux takes the size from the device
tree, which describes 16 MiB. This configuration is for the 32 MiB board.

Signed-off-by: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Upstream: not applicable (board variant)
---
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/espressif/esp32s31.dts
@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@
 
 	memory@50000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
-		reg = <0x50000000 0x01000000>;
+		reg = <0x50000000 0x02000000>;
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
